# mithraa.SHI — environment template
#
# The screens read NO environment variables. The only reads are in
# lib/supabase/*, which nothing imports yet (Phase 1A).
# `npm install && npm run dev` works with no env file at all.
#
# Everything below is OPTIONAL and read by the Next.js framework / CLI only,
# not by this project's code. Copy to `.env.local` if you want to set any.
#
# When a real backend is added (Project Brain database, AI providers, auth),
# add its variables here grouped by service, with REPLACE_WITH_* placeholders.
# Never put real values in this file.

# Vercel: no environment variables are required for Preview or Production.
#
# The server port is NOT read from .env files (verified on Next 16.4.2). Use
# `npm run dev -- -p 3001` or set PORT in the shell before `npm start`.

# --- Supabase (Project Brain, Phase 1A) --------------------------------------
# Read only by lib/supabase/*, which no screen imports yet; the app still runs
# without them. For local work, copy API_URL and PUBLISHABLE_KEY from
# `supabase status -o env`. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are sent to the browser, so
# only the publishable key belongs here. Secret / service_role keys must never
# get a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and are not used by the app.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=REPLACE_WITH_SUPABASE_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_PUBLISHABLE_KEY

# --- Next.js CLI (optional) --------------------------------------------------
# Opt out of anonymous Next.js telemetry (1 = disabled). Verified to work from
# .env.local for `next build` (dotenv loads before telemetry starts).
# NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1
